    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_MEGA_MHC_PREFILL=1` (opt-in; off by default) runs the DeepGEMM Mega-mHC boundary for every forward with at least one row, including decode and target-verify graphs. On a CC 10.7 node with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash DEP4, decode/verify is faster on the regular mHC path. There, the next sublayer's mix stats overlap the current sublayer on a side stream.\n\nMega-mHC is faster at every row count as a standalone kernel, so a row floor is the wrong gate. It would also push small prefix-hit extends to the slower path. The difference is the forward mode, not the size.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- On CC 10.7, Mega-mHC serves extends (and prefill graphs) of any size. Decode and target-verify take the regular path.\n- Other architectures keep today's behavior.\n- No new env var. The earlier `SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_MEGA_MHC_PREFILL_MIN_ROWS` revision is replaced.\n\nPairs with #46088: its fused decode post+combine sits behind the Mega-mHC branch in `_post_fusion`, so it only runs when Mega-mHC doesn't take the forward. That covers sm_107 decode with this PR.\n\n## Accuracy and speed\n\nOn a CC 10.7 node with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on the AgentX DEP4 recipe (DP attention + MegaMoE) with `SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_MEGA_MHC_PREFILL=1` opted in, arms ran in ABCCBA order within one job:\n- steady-state decode throughput at bs128 and bs224 improves over main, and further with #46088 enabled;\n- prefix-hit extends (1K/4K new tokens) and 128K prefill TTFT are unchanged;\n- GSM8K unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40593608628](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40593608628)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40593608601](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40593608601)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): 